      "title": "Wikipedia: Legal issues with service (latest year mentioned 2014)",
      "summary": "HireRight was the subject of a number of class-action and FCRA lawsuits. In 2011 the company paid $28 million to plaintiffs who accused HireRight of failing to provide copies of reports to job applicants and failing to resolve disputes. And on August 8, 2012, the US Department of Justice announced HireRight settled charges of violating the FCRA for $2.6M. Companies that use background check services must follow FCRA procedures or face class-action liability with millions of dollars in exposure. ...",
